  "feature_id": "F-64",
  "outcome": "SCR-03 Decision desk on the live API: read the invoice or accounting review, claim it, record approve, return or reject",
  "state": "IMPLEMENTING",
  "task_ids": [
    "FE-CONNECT-1"
  ],
  "operation_ids": [],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Open `/work/17/decide?task=41` against the mock or live server as a person who can claim. The page makes `GET /tasks/41`, one `POST /tasks/41/claim` with `{expected_revision:3}`, and shows the label, version, formatted amount and recipient \u2014 verify: network log in `tests/decide.test.tsx` (one claim call, even under StrictMode) and the page text.",
    "No evidence is pre-selected and approve, return and reject are disabled until one item of `review_evidence` is chosen \u2014 verify: test asserts disabled buttons on open, enabled after choosing, and the decision body carries that item's `id`.",
    "Approve sends exactly `{expected_revision, verdict:\"approve\", evidence_id, note}` with `note` present even when empty; return and reject with an empty note show a validation message and send nothing \u2014 verify: request-body assertions in the test.",
    "A decision 200 shows the done board with the verdict, note and label, and does not show \"decided by\" unless the history read has a matching item (then actor and time from it) \u2014 verify: test with and without a history item.",
    "A 409 on claim or decision reloads and shows the stale board with the replaced version beside the current one, controls on the current only after \"Review version n\"; the write is not resent \u2014 verify: test counts decision calls (1).",
    "A network or 5xx failure on the decision reloads once, never resends, and shows the uncertain notice; when the reload also fails, the buttons stay disabled and Try again only issues GETs \u2014 verify: test.",
    "Wrong user: `can_decide:false, can_claim:false` shows the read-only board with no decision controls and no specific reason sentence; no claim is sent \u2014 verify: test; wrong tenant or unknown task: GET 404 shows the no-access state; 401 shows signed-out; 403 on a write turns the page read-only \u2014 verify: tests per status.",
    "Invalid input: a 422 on the decision shows the server message (and `fields[]` text) without leaving the board and without clearing the picked evidence or note \u2014 verify: test.",
    "Unknown amount (`invoice_packet:null` or empty) shows \"Unknown\", never 0 or \"\u20a60.00\" \u2014 verify: test on `formatAmount` and the page.",
    "A task whose `verdicts[]` omits a verdict does not draw that button; no revoke control exists on SCR-03 or `InlineDecide` \u2014 verify: `grep -rn \"revoke\" src/features/decide src/features/workspace/InlineDecide.tsx` returns nothing, plus a test.",
    "No pager \"decision n of m\" is drawn unless `GET /work?queue=decisions` succeeds and contains this task; with the list failing the rest of the page still works \u2014 verify: test both cases.",
    "Comment on the not-yours board (if kept, Question 4) sends `{revision, body}`, requires a body, shows the server message on 403/409/422 and does not send twice \u2014 verify: test.",
    "Every call on this feature goes through `liveApi` and the typed live schema; `tests/api-live-schema-drift.test.ts` still passes \u2014 verify: `grep -rn \"api\\.\\(GET\\|POST\\)\" src/features/decide` returns nothing.",
    "The page matches the approved boards at 1440 and 390 for default, done, not-yours and stale, apart from the parts listed under Questions \u2014 verify: UI review of the changed area; the own board is checked only for the unreachable-state note below."
  ],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "surfaces": [
      "ui",
      "api",
      "contract-change",
      "product-decision"
    ],
    "rated_by": "readiness",
    "rationale": "Medium. The change is one screen, but it sits on a contract change: required evidence and note, no revoke, and reshaped task reads. It also writes a business decision (approval of an invoice or accounting review) with revision-conflict handling. Several design parts are removed because the live API cannot fill them, so the client must accept the result as a changed flow (product-decision). No data or migration work is involved, and the backend is not touched. Verification is contained: five boards and a mockable API."
  },
